a_per_play":0.06689,"pass_rate":0.6338,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6207,"def_epa_per_play":0.4132}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"MIN","distance":0.3636,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2021,"team":"LV","distance":0.3703,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.4339,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Brian Schottenheimer"},{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.4373,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":0.4382,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"CHI","distance":0.6472,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"LAC","distance":0.7723,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Brandon Staley"},{"season":2020,"team":"PHI","distance":0.7939,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"DET","distance":0.7987,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"HOU","distance":0.8172,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Falcons went 4-12 in 2020 and were outscored 414 to 396. The offense ranked 16th in EPA per play and the defense 21st in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. Their most distinctive trait was the lowest Cover 4 rate in the league.","offense":"The Falcons offense was about average by EPA per play, and it was much better passing the ball than running it. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Matt Ryan ran the passing game, with Calvin Ridley leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Falcons defense was a little below average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 4th and 26th. Grady Jarrett was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Deion Jones, who had 4.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Schematically, they had the lowest Cover 4 rate in the league.","special":"The Falcons were one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 50% of their short-yardage chances in normal situations. Their kickers made 95% of field goals, which was one of the best in the league. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their quarterbacks were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Matt Ryan played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,581 yards. Calvin Ridley was the clear top target with 24% of the looks and 1,374 receiving yards. The backfield was a committee led by Todd Gurley and Brian Hill. On defense, Deion Jones led the team with 4.5 sacks and Blidi Wreh-Wilson picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Vikings under Kevin O'Connell and the 2021 Raiders. Their defense looked most like the 2022 Bears and the 2023 Chargers under Brandon Staley.","trends":"The offense went from 15th in EPA per play in 2019 to 16th in 2020, about where it was. The defense moved from 22nd in EPA allowed per play in 2019 to 21st in 2020, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 22% to 7%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2020. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}